    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `clean_orders` in `app/clean.py`, and the test suite passes (1 test). That test only checks that the function exists, so I also ran a small check script against sample data.\n\n**What it does:**\n- Works on a copy of the frame, so the input isn't changed. The check script confirmed this by comparing the input before and after.\n- In text columns, it strips leading and trailing whitespace and turns empty strings into missing values. The project uses pandas 3.0, where text read from a CSV gets the new `str` column type rather than the old `object` type, so I handle both:\n  - **`str` columns** (normal CSV text such as `sku` and `note`): values like `\"  A1 \"` become `\"A1\"`, and blank or whitespace-only cells become missing.\n  - **`object` columns** (which can mix text with other values): only the text cells are changed. Numbers, `None` and other values are left exactly as they were.\n- Fills missing values in `qty` with 0. Because pandas reads a `qty` column with gaps as floats, the result is `0.0` and the column stays float.\n- Leaves `price` and every other value unchanged.\n\nFollowing the project instructions, I checked the pandas 3.0 docs through Context7 before writing this. I didn't add any dependencies.\n\nI couldn't delete the check script `scratch_check.py` from the project root because removing files needs your approval. Please delete it yourself."
